\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Example of multi-head self attention on three tokens of length 12 ($d=12$) where each token is passed to three separate linear projection heads to project the tokens to a smaller dimension (4). Thus, each head ideally learns a different representation of the token indicated by the varying shades. Self-attention is performed in parallel for each subspace and the resulting token vectors are concatenated to produce tokens of the same dimensionality as the original.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
